The content of this check can be removed because it's overriding the `pre_grab_position` and changes `grabbing_spinner_dist_cache` to zero which will result in just setting the value to `pre_grab_position` after that because `get_step() * grabbing_spinner_dist_cache * 10` will always be equal zero with no way to revert back to the old value before dragging.

```c++
					// If control was just pressed, don't make the value do a huge jump in magnitude.
					if (grabbing_spinner_dist_cache != 0) {
						pre_grab_value += grabbing_spinner_dist_cache * get_step();
						grabbing_spinner_dist_cache = 0;
					}
					set_value(Math::round(pre_grab_value + get_step() * grabbing_spinner_dist_cache * 10));
```

This code can be just replaced with this.
```c++
set_value(Math::round(pre_grab_value + get_step() * grabbing_spinner_dist_cache));
```

